[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3 uid="uid://bgubmaprange01"]

; Glowworm Grounds — the seventh map, and the first one that is not an arena
; (D-113). The practice range: a cleared bog at golden hour with a lodge at the south
; end, three throwing lanes, a sixty-metre bow lane, a gallery, a melee pit, an
; ability yard, a parkour course and void off the north and east edges.
;
; Like Kopje Crossing, Lantern Wharf, Halcyon Wake and Twin Quarry this scene
; has no geometry in it at all. `scripts/world/maps/range_map.gd` extends
; `StaticMap` and builds the whole place in `_ready()` from its layout tables,
; then calls `super()`, which sweeps it into world-space trimesh collision on
; layer 1, and then adds the dressing: ten torches, twenty-four glowworm
; lanterns, the MegaKit reed and snag, and the ambience.
;
; It also builds every `Marker3D` on the map in code rather than here, which is
; a departure from the other five and is deliberate. This map carries fifty-odd
; markers across eight groups, and every one of their positions is *derived* —
; a dummy stands on the distance mark its own post is generated from, a board
; stands `BOARD_OFFSET` off the lane centre the fences are generated from. Typed
; into a scene file those would be fifty coordinates that go stale silently the
; first time a lane moves. Built from the same tables as the geometry, they
; cannot.
;
; So this file is what `static_map.gd` asks for, and no more:
;
;   Environment  golden hour over the bog, at a fog density you can shoot
;                through (`range_env.tres`). See that file for why the ambient
;                went from 8.0 to 0.62 when the sky changed.
;   Sun          **nine degrees up and north-north-east** — thirty degrees east
;                of north — at 4.2 energy in a warm orange. The sky's disc
;                follows this node (`sun_follow_light` in `range_sky.tres`), so
;                what you can see in the sky and where the shadows point can
;                never disagree. Serialised ROW-major, as every `.tscn` stores a
;                `Transform3D`: the nine floats are the basis's three **rows**,
;                not its columns, and the axes are the columns. Written as
;                columns this node came out 59.6 degrees from where it was meant
;                to be — 7.8 degrees up and 30 degrees *west* of north — and the
;                error was silent because the moon it replaced was due north,
;                where the matrix is symmetric and the transpose is itself. The
;                light's own -Z — where the light *goes* — is
;                (-0.494, -0.156, +0.855), so the sun sits at
;                (+0.494, +0.156, -0.855): 9.0 degrees of elevation on a bearing
;                30.0 degrees east of north. `range_map._check_sun_and_sky`
;                prints both back out of the built scene and the gate reads them,
;                because this is exactly the kind of number that is wrong in a
;                way no render obviously shows.
;
;                This was an 11-degree moon due north at 1.15 in cold blue, and
;                the two changes are one decision (see `range_env.tres`): a
;                range you cannot read the ground of is not a range, and the
;                night's answer to that was to keep raising the fill until the
;                peat appeared. The hour before it gives the light for nothing.
;                **4.2 and not 2.0**: at 2.0 the warm key lost the argument with
;                the pink ambient and the whole bog came out mauve. The peat at
;                45 m now medians 82-126 of 255 with mean RGB 186/122/72 across
;                the four front pads.
;   Bounce       a second, shadowless directional light from the south-south-west
;                at -6 degrees. See the node.
;
;   Spawns       filled by the script: eight pads on the lodge deck, two rows of
;                four, all facing north up the range. The deck is 24 m wide
;                because `preview_map.PAD_SEPARATION` is 6 m and eight pads have
;                to fit on it.
;   Bases        built by the script at (-20, 0, 30) and (20, 0, 30), symmetric
;                about x = 0 so `CaptureLayout` splits the deck's eight pads four
;                and four rather than by a handful of centimetres (D-051).
;   Letters      B in the bow lane, O out in the ability yard, G between the
;                gallery and the pit.
;
; `void_height` is -12: the ground simply stops at the north and east lips and a
; fall from it takes 0.86 s, which is a lesson rather than a wait. The melee pit
; floor at -1.5 has ten and a half metres of clearance under it, so nobody dies
; by walking into the melee ring.
;
; ## Nine degrees, and thirty degrees east of north
;
; Both numbers are the renders' doing, and the second one is the one with an
; argument under it.
;
; **Elevation.** Seven degrees puts cos(83) — twelve per cent — of a light's
; energy onto a horizontal surface, and a horizontal surface is what this entire
; map is made of. Eleven put nineteen per cent down and was chosen for that.
; Nine is a step back toward the horizon and it is bought with the sky rather
; than paid for by the ground: sin(9) is 15.6% down, but the fill is now a lit
; dome instead of a night, so the peat is brighter at nine degrees than it ever
; was at eleven. What nine buys over eleven is the picture — the glory sits
; lower, the cumulus are lit further up their flanks, and the shadows get long
; enough to be scenery.
;
; **Azimuth, and this is the load-bearing one.** A shadow from a 9-degree light
; is **6.31 times as long as the thing casting it** (1 / tan 9). The west bank is
; 8 m of peat running the full 90 m length of the map, so it throws a
; **50.5 m** shadow, and where that lands is entirely a question of the bearing:
;
;   north-north-west  (the first attempt, D-113) — 41 m of shadow laid *across*
;                     a 60 m map. Two thirds of the range in permanent darkness,
;                     and no amount of ambient fixes a shadow.
;   due north         (what shipped) — the bank shadows along its own length and
;                     therefore shadows nothing, and so do the lane fences, which
;                     run the same way. It also puts the disc at the vanishing
;                     point of every lane, which is a sun in the crosshair of an
;                     archer at the firing line.
;   north-north-east  (here) — shadows run **south-south-west**, on (-0.5, +0.866).
;                     The bank's 50.5 m goes 25.2 m west and 43.7 m south: west
;                     is *off the map* (the bank is already the west edge) and
;                     south runs out under the lodge. It shadows nothing, for the
;                     same reason due north did, and it does it while standing
;                     30 degrees off every lane's axis.
;
; Everything else follows: the lodge ridge at 7.4 m throws 46.7 m, 40 m of it
; southward, off the south edge of the world; the south banks do the same; the
; 3 m yard ledge throws 18.9 m into open yard; a 2.2 m distance post throws
; 13.9 m diagonally across a 6 m lane, which is a stripe of texture on the peat
; and the reason the ground reads as ground rather than as paint. The 0.60 m lane
; rails throw 3.8 m and are the only shadows in a lane a thrower can see past.
;
; And the crosshair. The lanes run due north; the sun is 30 degrees east of it.
; A half-horizontal FOV at 16:9 is about 54 degrees, so the glory is **in frame
; and ahead-right of the crosshair** from every firing line, and the disc is
; nowhere near the target. That was the brief: sky glory down the lane, not a
; disc in the sight.
;
; The cost, stated, and it is the same trade D-113 made: the faces a shooter
; sees are the *south-south-west* ones, which are the shaded ones. That is the
; right way round for a range — a target read as a shape against a bright sky is
; a target you can lead at forty-five metres — and the ambient is what keeps its
; near face from being a hole.
;
; `tools/preview_map.gd` stands a Bog on every pad, `tools/parkour_report.gd`
; walks the jump graph and proves the course and the off-limits tops, and
; `tools/playthrough.gd -- range` runs the practice branch and plans the capture
; layout off the declared bases.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/world/maps/range_map.gd" id="1_range_map"]
[ext_resource type="Environment" path="res://resources/config/range_env.tres" id="2_range_env"]

[node name="Range" type="Node3D"]
script = ExtResource("1_range_map")
void_height = -12.0
base_radius = 4.0

[node name="Environment" type="WorldEnvironment" parent="."]
